# File: tests/blender/test_meshy_session.py (SCN001–SCN003), tests/bdd/features/meshy.feature (SCN004)
# Generated from: specs/105-normalize-meshy-glb-imports-to-a-welded-mesh-with-the-origin-at-the-bottom-center/requirements.md
Feature: Meshy GLB imports arrive welded, bottom-centered, and smooth-shaded

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Seam-split vertices are welded
    Given a GLB of a UV-seamed cube whose exporter split its vertices at the seams
    When import_glb imports it as "Crate"
    Then SM_Crate is one connected island
    And its face count, per-corner UVs, and material slots match the source cube

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The origin is at the bottom center
    Given a GLB of a cube placed at (2, 3, 4)
    When import_glb imports it as "Crate"
    Then SM_Crate has identity location, rotation, and scale
    And its bounding box X and Y center and minimum Z are within 0.001 m of 0

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Custom normals are replaced by smoothing by angle
    Given a GLB of a cube with custom split normals
    When import_glb imports it as "Crate"
    Then SM_Crate has no custom split normals
    And its faces are smooth with edges sharper than 30 degrees marked sharp
    And every face normal points away from the cube's center

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The import and job results report the normalization
    Given a Meshy generate job whose session import succeeds
    When the job finishes
    Then the import result and the job result carry merged_vertices and origin_offset
